n HTTP 200 with all matching requests ordered by createdAt descending (with no required relative order for equal timestamps), HTTP 400 with the contract ErrorResponse for malformed or unsupported status filters, and HTTP 500 with message \\\"Could not load requests.\\\" for list failures.\",\n  \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n  \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n  \"sources\": [\n   \"I-1\"\n  ],\n  \"stability\": 1\n },\n {\n  \"acceptance\": [\n   {\n    \"given\": \"The database is available and contains no request matching the submitted data.\",\n    \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n    \"level\": \"api\",\n    \"then\": \"The response status is 201; the returned record has a positive system-generated id, UTC createdAt, trimmed title and description, status field \\\"Open\\\", and only fields allowed by the MaintenanceRequest schema; caller-supplied system-controlled values are not used.\",\n    \"when\": \"A client posts a valid request with padded title and description and valid caller-supplied id, createdAt, and status values.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"given\": \"The database is available and the request body has a valid title, area, and priority.\",\n    \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n    \"level\": \"api\",\n    \"then\": \"Both response statuses are 201 and neither returned resource has a description field.\",\n    \"when\": \"A client posts a valid request once without description and once with a description that is blank after trimming.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"given\": \"The database operation for creating a valid request fails after startup.\",\n    \"id\": \"AC-2.3\",\n    \"level\": \"api\",\n    \"then\": \"The response status is 500 and the response message is \\\"Could not create the request.\\\"\",\n    \"when\": \"A client posts the request.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"ears\": \"When a client sends a valid POST /api/requests body, the Maintenance Requests API shall create and return HTTP 201 with a positive system-assigned id, UTC createdAt, trimmed title and description, and Open status, ignore caller-suppli